      { q: 'How can I buy Bitcoin?', a: 'You can buy Bitcoin through a cryptocurrency exchange or directly with a regulated broker like Orion Capital. Simply create and verify an account, deposit funds, and place your first trade.' },
      { q: 'Are Bitcoin transactions anonymous?', a: 'Not entirely. Bitcoin is pseudonymous — transactions are recorded publicly on the blockchain and linked to wallet addresses rather than names, so with enough analysis they can often be traced back to individuals.' },
      { q: 'How many Bitcoins are there?', a: 'Bitcoin’s supply is capped at 21 million coins. New bitcoins are created through mining, and roughly every four years the mining reward is halved, slowing issuance over time.' },
      { q: 'What happens when all Bitcoins are mined?', a: 'No new bitcoins will be created, and miners will earn income solely from transaction fees. The network is expected to keep operating as normal, secured by fee-paying transactions.' },
